        <!-- ================================================================
             TRAINING FAQ
             ================================================================ -->

        <section class="r154-training-section" id="training-faq" aria-labelledby="training-faq-title">

            <div class="r154-training-section-heading">

                <span class="r154-training-eyebrow">
                    Common Course and Registration Questions
                </span>

                <h2 class="r154-training-section-title" id="training-faq-title">
                    Training &amp; Events FAQ
                </h2>

            </div>


            <div class="r154-training-faq-grid">

                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Which course should a completely new referee take?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Select Regional Referee Full In-Person or complete the
                        Regional Referee online course plus an approved
                        Companion Field Day.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Must I take both new-referee options?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        No. Choose the complete full in-person course or the
                        online-plus-companion pathway.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Who should take the Intermediate course?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        It is intended for current Regional Referees pursuing
                        the Intermediate Referee badge.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        May a youth referee attend the Regional course?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Yes. Youth referees use the Regional Referee pathway,
                        subject to the youth-volunteer registration and parent
                        requirements.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        How do I access AYSOU?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Sign in to the Region 154 SportsConnect website and
                        select the AYSOU button connected to your volunteer
                        record.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Can I use a direct AYSOU username and password?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Access AYSOU through SportsConnect single sign-on so
                        training remains connected to the correct volunteer
                        record.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        What should I do when a prerequisite is missing?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Save the completion certificate or screenshot and
                        contact referee leadership before attending.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        May I attend training offered by another region?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Yes, when it is the correct AYSO course and you enroll
                        through AYSOU. Confirm the selection with the RRA when
                        uncertain.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        What happens when a course is full?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Search AYSOU and the Area E schedule for another
                        approved date or contact the RRA for guidance.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Must I stay for the entire course?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Referee certification courses require completion of all
                        required instructional and practical components.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        Where are annual Law changes explained?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Review Rules &amp; Learning and attend the returning-
                        referee meeting for current Region guidance.
                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-training-faq-card">

                    <h3>
                        What happens after I complete the course?
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Confirm that the certification appears in your record,
                        then contact the RRA about equipment, mentoring and an
                        appropriate assignment.
                    </p>

                </article>

            </div>


